welcome back to the David Pakman show  I'm fair and cousins from Ring of Fire  sitting in for David Pakman today you  can follow me on twitter at fair and  balanced you also find me on instagram  and facebook at that same handle at fair  and balanced we've got a little bit more  Trump news to talk about today because  the man got a little bit more bad news  yesterday and that bad news came in the  form of a court ruling by Judge Amit  Mehta  who said that I'm sorry Donald and Trump  administration but I'm not going to  block the Democrats request to get your  financial documents now if you rewind  the clock about a week ago when the  Trump administration made these  arguments in court in front of Judge  Metta judge Mehta at the time basically  told Trump's lawyers that your arguments  don't hold any water because the Trump  lawyers were trying to say Democrats  can't request Donald Trump's financial  documents because it's not related to  any legislation that they're trying to  pass and Congress's job as we all know  is only to pass legislation and the  judge said no no really it's not that's  not how the separation of powers work  they actually also have oversight  authority of the executive branch and so  this would fall within the things  they're legally allowed to do even if  it's not related to legislation but then  the judge said but listen I understand  the importance of this and I'm gonna  weigh both sides of the argument so I'm  gonna look at all the evidence and I'm  gonna take some time before I hand down  this ruling because I don't want to rush  it  that was the mature responsible  professional and legally correct thing  for this judge to do and then Monday  hands down the ruling he says yeah  Republicans I thought about it and  listen your arguments they were garbage  they don't work they don't hold up it  flies in the face of the separation of  powers and so yes  therefore the Democrats 100% can get  their hands on Donald Trump's financial  records now Trump immediately got angry  he told reporters he's gonna appeal it  and he's furious that this Obama  a judge he kept calling him and Obama  appointed judge in fact one point he  said it was a recently appointed Obama  Obama judge recently so yes Obama came  out of retirement while Trump was  President to go ahead just to point this  judge the guy's been out of office for  two and a half years that's not exactly  recent Trump but nonetheless yeah  Obama did appoint this judge and this  judge 100% did what any normal  well-respected person who understands  the law would do and they smacked down  your lawyers because their argument was  absolute garbage you know there is one  theme that's developing throughout the  Trump administration and we've seen it  unfold very publicly and that is the  fact that this man has some of the worst  lawyers imaginable I mean think about it  Michael Cohen he's in jail now he will  be for the next three years Rudy  Giuliani that man actually went on TV  multiple different times and implicated  Donald Trump in crimes and that was  supposed to be his client Jay Sekulow  well we all know the story that emerged  yesterday we're going to talk about that  a little bit later in the bonus show but  Jay Sekulow apparently ordered Michael  Cohen to lie to Congress and then you  have these bonehead lawyers who go into  court acting like they don't understand  the roles that Congress constitutionally  has and the judge has to say listen you  don't seem to understand how Congress  works but they're allowed to do this  so yeah Trump clearly has a history of  hiring horrible people to be his lawyers  and to that I say please continue this  it's a lot of fun watching your lawyers  going to court and reading these filings  and seeing how clueless they are and how  desperate they are to protect whatever  it is you're hiding so please continue  to hire from the bottom of the barrel  because it's making life for the rest of  us so much more entertaining but to the  actual ruling right I am NOT just the  ruling from the judge but what it means  it means as of right now but course  Trump's gonna appeal it Democrats could  get their hands on the financial records  and the big question is  obviously what the heck is Donald Trump  hiding you know he also claimed after  going after this quote Obama appointed  judge that he has had the most  transparent administration in history  he's either completely delusional or he  thinks everybody in this country is an  absolute idiot if he thinks he can get  away with saying that we can't see his  grades from college or high school we  can't see his medical records we can't  see his tax returns we can't see his  financial records we can't see his  business holdings there is nothing  transparent about Donald Trump except  his hair but nonetheless he is hiding  something  that much is pretty obvious right folks  you don't go through all of this wreck  effort you don't threaten to sue schools  if they release your grades if you're  not trying to hide something you don't  fight congressional subpoenas in court  unless you're trying to prevent Congress  from seeing something you don't want  them to see the big question is what is  he hiding is he hiding bank fraud well  representative Ted Lew made a pretty  strong case during Michael Cohen's  testimony to Congress that Donald Trump  committed bank fraud and based on the  cooperation that Deutsche Bank has had  so far with congressional Democrats it  seems pretty obvious that he inflated  his net worth in order to secure a loan  that's fraud you can't do that is there  potential money laundering now again the  folks at Deutsche Bank really seemed to  think that there was not just with Trump  but with Jared Kushner so there's that  but I think the biggest thing this man  wants to hide because I think he thinks  he can get away with any criminal  activity that doesn't bother him never  has never will as a man who's gotten  away with quite literally everything for  his entire life but what he can't get  away with is destroying his reputation  I think these financial documents would  tell us that Donald Trump does not have  as much money as he says he has and if  that were to be the case that would  absolutely destroy the image that  he has spent his entire life crafting  and there's no coming back from that you  know he could do his best to lie his way  out of criminal activity  he's already lied his way about out of  the fact that he lost all that money you  know trying to say that oh no it was  just she kind of write these numbers and  it's almost fraud but it's totally not  fraud and everybody did it except I  didn't actually do that so you did lose  the money all he did was just spew out a  bunch of words further confusing the  public and suddenly everybody split on  whether or not the man did lose the  money or if he committed fraud or if he  did pay taxes or what the hell's going  on nobody knows so he thinks he can lie  his way out of criminal activity is all  I'm trying to say but he can't lie his  way out of the fact that he may not have  as much money as he wants us to think he  does and that would destroy him it  wouldn't end his presidency but it would  absolutely deliver a blow to his ego  that I do not know this man would ever  be able to physically and emotionally  overcome because that is the thing that  matters the most to him yes this man  loves money more than I have ever seen a  human being love money but that money is  what made that ego and if we find out  that the money's not there then suddenly  his lifetime of lies creating this  facade comes crumbling to the ground and  this man would never be able to recover  from that

